Question Bank
============
1. Short-Answer Questions (Theory & Concepts) - 2 to 5-mark questions 
a. What are the primary differences between User Interface (UI) and User Experience (UX) design?
b. List and explain the 5 stages of the Design Thinking process.
c. What is the purpose of wireframing in the design process?
d. Explain the 7 Golden Rules of UI design (e.g., consistency, preventing errors, informative feedback).
e. What are User Personas, and why are they important in user-centered design?
f. What does "Information Architecture" mean in web and app design? [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

2. Long-Answer Questions (Processes & Evaluation) - 10 to 15-mark questions 
a. Describe a complete UX design process from initial user research to final hand-off.
b. How do you conduct usability testing? Explain the steps involved and the goals of this phase.
c. Explain how you would perform a heuristic evaluation on a live website or application.
d. Discuss the significance of Accessibility (WCAG guidelines) in digital product design. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

3. Practical / Lab Design Assignments (Skill-based)
   Practical or lab-based BCA exams, using industry-standard tools like Figma: 
•	Design a responsive layout for a Location-Based Services app or an E-Commerce platform using Figma.
•	Conduct a Design Thinking process for an online Ticket Reservation system (create user personas, storyboards, and wireframes).
•	Create a UI Style Guide (defining color palettes, typography scaling, and button states) for a Healthcare Application. [1, 2, 3]


